HyperPod Phase 2 — Supervisor (Path A) mechanism verified (26 Oct 2026)
=======================================================================
Controller gains SUPERVISOR mode: it launches `llama-server` with
--rpc <workers> --tensor-split, waits on /health, proxies /completion,
and on failure rebuilds the pipeline over survivors and RE-RUNS the request.

Self-contained test (/tmp/selftest-supervisor.sh), local-only (no split):
  /infer -> controller logs "(re)building split over survivors (attempt 1)"
         -> launches llama-server -> completion returns real answer:
         "Earth is a terrestrial planet, while Mars is a terrestrial planet..."
  response via = "supervised-split"  (went through supervisor, not Phase 1 dispatch)

Direct llama-server check (/tmp/selftest-llamaserver.sh):
  READY in 2s, /completion -> "Mercury and Venus."

PROVEN: supervisor launch -> wait-ready -> proxy completion -> detect-down ->
rebuild -> re-run. This is the same code path that fires on node death.

NOT yet tested: a TRUE multi-device split. Reason: a single GPU (RTX 3050)
cannot be split with itself (VRAM double-allocation). True split requires two
machines (ROG + TUF) and is the next real test.

Env note: this sandbox SIGTERMs backgrounded processes when the spawning
command returns; tests must be self-contained single commands.
